              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Factorise using the intercepts and differentiate. The tangents have equal and opposite gradients because the parabola is symmetric about the midpoint of the intercepts.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "\n\n$$\\begin{align*}f(x)&=a(x-\\alpha)(x-\\beta)\\\\f'(x)&=a(2x-\\alpha-\\beta)\\\\f'(\\alpha)&=a(\\alpha-\\beta)\\\\f'(\\beta)&=a(\\beta-\\alpha)\\\\f'(\\alpha)+f'(\\beta)&=a(\\alpha-\\beta)+a(\\beta-\\alpha)=0.\\end{align*}$$\n\n The parabola is symmetric about $x=\\dfrac{\\alpha+\\beta}{2}$, so its tangents at the two intercepts have equal and opposite gradients.",
